<LegalLayout
  pageTitle="Cancellation & Rescheduling Policy · Pro Se Fair Play Mediation"
  description="When a mediation session is confirmed, how much notice is required to cancel or reschedule, what happens when only one party cancels, and how no-shows, technology failures and hurricanes are handled."
  kicker="Policies"
  title="Cancellation &amp;"
  titleItalic="rescheduling"
  effective="August 28, 2026"
  version="1.0"
  lede="Mediation is two people agreeing to be in the same room at the same time. That is harder to arrange than it sounds, which is why the notice terms below exist — and why the aim is almost always to move a session rather than cancel it."
>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">Reserved professional time</h2>
      <p>
        A mediation session involves reserved professional time, scheduling
        coordination between two parties, and advance preparation. That time
        cannot usually be reassigned on short notice, which is the reason a
        cancellation close to a session carries a cost where an early one does
        not.
      </p>
      <p>
        The goal of this policy is to reschedule rather than to refund. By the
        time two people reach mediation they have already agreed to sit down
        together, and finding the next set of hours that suits both of them is
        almost always the better outcome. Refunds are set out on the
        <a href="/refund">Refund Policy</a> page.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">When a session is confirmed</h2>
      <p>
        A session is reserved only once payment has been received in full. Where
        the fee is being split between the parties, the session is confirmed only
        when <strong>both</strong> parties' payments have been received. A
        calendar hold without payment does not reserve the time.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">Notice required to cancel or reschedule</h2>
      <h3 class="section-h3">More than 24 hours' notice</h3>
      <p>
        Cancellations or rescheduling requests made more than twenty-four (24)
        hours before a scheduled session are eligible for either:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>a full refund to the original payment method, or</li>
        <li>a full session credit to be applied toward a future mediation session.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="section-h3">Less than 24 hours' notice</h3>
      <p>
        Fifty percent (50%) of the mediation retainer is retained as a reserved
        session and preparation fee. The remaining balance may be applied as a
        one-time credit toward a session rescheduled within thirty (30) days,
        subject to availability.
      </p>

      <h3 class="section-h3">Failure to appear</h3>
      <p>
        A party who does not appear for a scheduled session, and gives no notice,
        forfeits the full mediation retainer. A party who has not joined within
        twenty (20) minutes of the start time, having given no notice, may be
        treated as a no-show.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">When only one party cancels</h2>
      <p>
        A mediation session requires the participation of both parties. A
        cancellation or non-appearance by either party is treated as a
        cancellation of the session as a whole, and the notice provisions above
        apply to the session, not to each party separately.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where the fee has been split, any amount retained under this policy is
        applied proportionally to each party's payment, and any credit is issued
        to the paying parties in the same proportions. Where one party has paid
        the full session fee, any retained amount and any credit belong to that
        party.
      </p>
      <h3 class="section-h3">Where the other party declines to proceed</h3>
      <p>
        Mediation begins only after both parties agree to proceed. If the other
        party declines to participate, or does not confirm within a reasonable
        period, the paying party receives a <strong>full refund</strong>,
        regardless of the notice periods above. Nobody should be out of pocket
        because the person they hoped to mediate with said no.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">Session length, overruns and late arrival</h2>
      <p>
        Sessions are booked in reserved blocks. If a session concludes earlier
        than scheduled, the reserved time has been held for you and the balance
        is not refunded.
      </p>
      <p>
        Time beyond the booked block continues at the applicable hourly rate in
        thirty (30) minute increments, and only where both parties and the
        mediator agree to continue.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sessions begin at the scheduled time. A late arrival does not extend the
        block.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">Courtesy rescheduling</h2>
      <p>
        One courtesy reschedule may be accommodated for unforeseen circumstances,
        provided reasonable notice is given and scheduling availability permits.
        Emergency situations and unforeseen events are considered on a
        case-by-case basis.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">If the mediator cancels or declines the matter</h2>
      <p>
        If a session is cancelled or rescheduled by the mediator, you may choose a
        full refund or a full session credit, regardless of notice.
      </p>
      <p>
        If, after payment, the mediator determines that mediation is not
        appropriate for your matter — including where screening indicates
        coercion, a safety concern, or a conflict of interest — the engagement is
        ended and all fees for unperformed work are refunded in full. If the
        mediator must withdraw during a matter, any prepaid time not yet used is
        refunded.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">Remote sessions and technology</h2>
      <p>
        Sessions are conducted by Zoom. If a session cannot proceed, or must be
        cut short, because of a failure on the mediator's side — connection,
        platform or equipment — it is rescheduled at no charge, or the affected
        time is refunded or credited at your election.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each party is responsible for their own device, connection and a private
        space in which to participate. Where a party's own connectivity prevents
        them from taking part, the session is treated under the cancellation
        provisions above.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">Events beyond anyone's control</h2>
      <p>
        Where a session cannot proceed because of a hurricane, tropical storm,
        evacuation order, extended utility or internet outage, or another event
        beyond the reasonable control of either party, it is rescheduled at no
        charge and no cancellation fee applies. In South Florida this is a when
        rather than an if, and it is not held against anyone.
      </p>
      <h2 class="display section-h2">Document preparation</h2>
      <p>
        Parenting Plan Preparation and the Turn-Key Court Packet are flat-fee
        document services rather than scheduled sessions, so the notice periods on
        this page do not apply to them. Their terms are on the
        <a href="/refund">Refund Policy</a> page.
      </p>
</LegalLayout>
